---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---
<PageLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="How AI Founder Files handles personal data under UK GDPR."
  label="Privacy"
  heading="Privacy policy"
>
  <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> 4 October 2026</p>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} (“we”, “us”) is a UK-based publication. We are the data controller for personal data collected through this website. Contact: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Newsletter subscribers:</strong> your email address, the date and time you subscribed, which form you used, and that you ticked the consent box. We record when emails are sent to you and when you unsubscribe or an address bounces.</li>
    <li><strong>Emails you send us:</strong> your email address and whatever you tell us.</li>
    <li><strong>Server logs:</strong> our hosting provider (Vercel) processes technical data such as IP address and browser type to deliver the site and keep it secure.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>This site doesn’t currently use analytics, advertising or tracking cookies. If that changes, we’ll update this page first.</p>

  <h2>Why we use it, and our lawful basis</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To send you the weekly newsletter: <strong>your consent</strong> (UK GDPR Article 6(1)(a)). You can withdraw it at any time.</li>
    <li>To reply to your emails and handle correction requests: <strong>legitimate interests</strong> (Article 6(1)(f)).</li>
    <li>To keep the site secure and running: <strong>legitimate interests</strong> (Article 6(1)(f)).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>
    We use Supabase to store the subscriber list, Twilio SendGrid to send the newsletter and welcome email, Vercel to host the site, and GitHub to run the weekly send. They process data on our behalf under their own terms. We don’t sell your data. Some of these providers are based in, or process data in, the United States. Where that happens, the transfer is covered by an approved safeguard such as the UK–US data bridge or the UK’s standard contractual clauses.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    We keep your subscription details for as long as you are subscribed. If you unsubscribe, we keep only your email address and the date you unsubscribed, on a suppression list, so that we never email you again. If you would rather we erased that too, email us and we’ll delete it from our database and from our email provider. Emails you send us are kept for as long as needed to deal with your request.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You have the right to access your data, have it corrected or deleted, restrict or object to its use, withdraw consent, and ask for a copy in a portable format. To use these rights, email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>. You can also complain to the Information Commissioner’s Office (<a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" rel="noopener noreferrer">ico.org.uk</a>) if you are unhappy with how we handle your data.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>We’ll update this page when our practices change and revise the date at the top.</p>
</PageLayout>
